@c ===================================================================
@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@command{rl} is the command-line interface for the rl programming language.
It provides tools for running, checking, scaffolding, formatting, and
packaging rl source files, plus a package manager.

Compiling to bytecode, transpiling to C, the interactive REPL, the language
server, the docs viewer, and the toolchain manager ship as separate
binaries: @command{rlc}, @command{rlt}, @command{rlrepl}, @command{rlsp},
@command{rldocs}, and @command{rlm}.

@c ===================================================================
@node Commands
@chapter Commands

@table @code
@item rl run @var{file} [@option{-c} @var{code}] [@option{--vm}] [@option{--} @var{args}...]
Lex, parse, and evaluate a @file{.rl} source file.

@item rl dev [@option{--vm}]
Run the current project by reading @file{rl.toml}.

@item rl new @var{name} [@option{--no-git}] [@option{--script}] [@option{--lib}]
Scaffold a new project directory or create a standalone script.

@item rl check @var{file}
Type-check a @file{.rl} file and report errors without running it.

@item rl format @var{file}
Format a @file{.rl} source file in place.

@item rl print @var{file} (@option{-t} | @option{-p} | @option{-a})
Print debug information for a @file{.rl} source file.

@item rl package @var{file} [@option{-o} @var{output}] [@option{--vm}]
Package a @file{.rl} file into a self-contained binary.

@item rl workflows @option{--check} | @option{--package}
Scaffold GitHub Actions workflow files.

@item rl pm @var{command}
Manage project dependencies (@code{install}, @code{add}, @code{remove},
@code{list}, @code{update}, @code{cache}).

@item rl test @var{file} [@option{--match} @var{pattern}] [@option{-c} @var{code}]
Discover and run @code{!#[test]} functions with setup/teardown hooks.
Tests never run under @command{rl run}.
@end table

@c ===================================================================
@node run Command
@chapter run Command

@command{rl run @var{file}} lexes, parses, and evaluates a @file{.rl} source
file. Arguments after the file path are passed to the script as its @code{argv}
array.

@section Options

@table @code
@item @option{-c} @var{code}, @option{--code} @var{code}
Execute inline rl code instead of a file.

@item @option{--vm}
Run through the bytecode VM (highly experimental).
@end table

@section Examples

@example
$ rl run hello.rl
$ rl run script.rl -- --verbose input.txt
$ rl run -c 'println("hello")'
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node dev Command
@chapter dev Command

@command{rl dev} runs the current project by reading @file{rl.toml} in the
current directory.

@section Options

@table @code
@item @option{--vm}
Run through the bytecode VM (highly experimental).
@end table

@section Examples

@example
$ rl dev
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node new Command
@chapter new Command

@command{rl new @var{name}} scaffolds a new project directory with the standard
structure and a @file{rl.toml} configuration file. Alternatively, with the
@option{--script} flag, it creates a single standalone @file{.rl} file.

@section Options

@table @code
@item @option{--no-git}
Skip running @command{git init} in the new project directory.

@item @option{--script}
Create a standalone @file{.rl} script instead of a project directory.

@item @option{--lib}
Create a library project (generates @file{src/lib.rl} instead of
@file{src/main.rl}).
@end table

@section Examples

@example
$ rl new my_project
$ rl new --script my_script
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node check Command
@chapter check Command

@command{rl check @var{file}} type-checks a @file{.rl} source file and
reports errors without running it.

@section Examples

@example
$ rl check script.rl
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node format Command
@chapter format Command

@command{rl format @var{file}} formats a @file{.rl} source file in place
according to the rl coding style.

@section Examples

@example
$ rl format script.rl
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node print Command
@chapter print Command

@command{rl print @var{file}} prints debug information for a @file{.rl}
source file. Exactly one of @option{--tokens}, @option{--parser}, or
@option{--ast} must be given.

@section Options

@table @code
@item @option{-t}, @option{--tokens}
Print the token stream from the lexer.

@item @option{-p}, @option{--parser}
Print the parsed AST (before type checking).

@item @option{-a}, @option{--ast}
Print the type-checked AST.
@end table

@section Examples

@example
$ rl print script.rl --tokens
$ rl print script.rl --parser
$ rl print script.rl --ast
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node package Command
@chapter package Command

@command{rl package @var{file}} packages a @file{.rl} file into a
self-contained binary. The @file{.rl} source text is embedded directly
into the compiled output.

@section Options

@table @code
@item @option{-o} @var{path}, @option{--output} @var{path}
Output binary path. Defaults to @code{program}.

@item @option{--vm}
Compile to @file{.rlc} bytecode first and embed that (compressed) instead
of the raw source text.
@end table

@section Examples

@example
$ rl package script.rl
$ rl package script.rl -o myapp
$ rl package script.rl --vm
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node workflows Command
@chapter workflows Command

@command{rl workflows} scaffolds GitHub Actions workflow files. At least
one of @option{--check} or @option{--package} must be given.

@section Options

@table @code
@item @option{--check}
Generate a workflow that runs @command{rl check} on push/PR.

@item @option{--package}
Generate a workflow that packages and releases a binary.
@end table

@section Examples

@example
$ rl workflows --check
$ rl workflows --package
$ rl workflows --check --package
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node pm Command
@chapter pm Command

@command{rl pm} manages project dependencies: it downloads tarballs,
verifies SHA256 hashes, and links them into @file{deps/}.

@section Examples

@example
$ rl pm install some-package
$ rl pm list
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node test Command
@chapter test Command

@command{rl test @var{file}} discovers @code{!#[test]} functions and runs
them with setup/teardown hooks, reporting pass/fail/skip with a non-zero
exit on failure.

@section Options

@table @code
@item @option{--match} @var{pattern}
Only run tests whose name, group, or register contains @var{pattern}.

@item @option{-c} @var{code}, @option{--code} @var{code}
Execute inline rl code instead of a file.
@end table

@section Examples

@example
$ rl test tests.rl
$ rl test tests.rl --match money
@end example

@c ===================================================================
@node Examples
@chapter Examples

@section Running a Script

@example
$ rl run hello.rl
Hello, world!
@end example

@section Running with Arguments

@example
$ rl run script.rl -- --verbose input.txt
@end example

@section Inline Code

@example
$ rl run -c 'println("hello")'
hello
@end example

@section Type Checking

@example
$ rl check script.rl
@end example

@section Running Tests

@example
$ rl test tests.rl
@end example

@section Formatting

@example
$ rl format script.rl
@end example

@section Compiling to Bytecode

@example
$ rlc compile script.rl -o output.rlc
@end example

@section Printing Tokens

@example
$ rl print script.rl --tokens
@end example

@section Transpiling to C

@example
$ rlt script.rl --runtime --compile
@end example

@section Packaging a Binary

@example
$ rl package script.rl -o myapp
@end example

@section Starting the REPL

@example
$ rlrepl
@end example

